<description>&lt;p&gt;Venezuela is moving to repeal the law that bars opposition figures from office and the Simón Bolívar law aimed at countering a U.S. blockade, while the National Assembly advances these changes. The WHO director-general visited for the first time and pledged health support, and the United States and Qatar are working to clear regional development bank arrears. China and Russia have lost oil footholds worth $22 billion, and a fire at the Amuay refinery was contained without affecting fuel supply. A tentative trial date was set for a soldier accused of profiting from Maduro's capture, and Iran rejected claims that Kuwait attacked it, warning of an Israeli plot. 2 battle-related deaths occurred in 2007, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipgFBVV95cUxOZk56U1ppNndqeTVWb2FvZ1ktaVRZTEx0WENYTEFCMVR2Q2huWnJBbG11ek5IUVVmaVJqUjItSDNmZDlaTVNGNjhoa09Wd1E1OXNKbG85WGVTZGpvVVVSYW1iZEc0alF4Q3ZFb1hqYXdrVFd5SjVjbnp0MDZlZVNZam5HY1M2czV1SHFSV0dIcUFvV3U2Q1FhT0I0MGF2UzlPd3FhRXVR?oc=5&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiyAFBVV95cUxNYnZ1a0tWZGRjN19GNkZNS0JoYmlDZGNHSkVZMmM1d2xsTEN1QmhsNkZtWVZfelZCUzdid05hSkVYa0hNVmpRazY0MUtWdWJQR2FydkFUeWtqZUotbXVvQ1JPVWg2Y0tGdWZOQ0hHUkNLRGh6Nm5SMjBNVldmRm1YZU1iaG5DSjdaSmFTcXpIdDZwUExwOFQzNWxSMk1QV1NaWWVONy02Y2FSa2xZbV8wUWMtd0h1clBxZ01aYTdpd0xYYjZMXzVrVQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMifEFVX3lxTE1UTzI4MWkwZTREeURlNlJ4NElRN2JwRmJ2Sy1aeTNWVEpqcjloeG8zRkFjMTJycXdZRkF2b1NmdnNUdjZHeEJIdDVXSW9qVHRjM1hOc2ZQUkVjTS01emp6ek5hTnA1NUtObVFjcmRZaklLMk52NlFmNlNjeFU?oc=5&quot;&gt;Latin Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxQUkFzNXQ2bmFKRGVZMXhoal